earlier) — not merely that the child started.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.3937,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1 requires the marker prove the child 'reached the write attempt' but only that it is emitted 'after starting' and asserted 'before the denial is read' — nothing forces the signal to be emitted at/after the denied operation.","The existing in-repo pattern _seatbelt_works() emits the marker FIRST: `echo {marker}; echo x > {target}` (mutation_sandbox.py:124) — copying that ordering proves only launch, not that the denied write line executed.","This re-creates, one layer deeper, the exact 'executed-and-denied vs never-ran' ambiguity the ticket exists to remove: launched-and-printed-but-crashed-before-the-write is neither."],"finding":"The plan pins that liveness must be asserted 'before the denial is read' and prove the child 'reached the write attempt', but it does not constrain the ORDER of the liveness signal relative to the denied operation, so a child that starts and emits its marker but then dies before attempting the denied write still shows liveness-present + artifact-absent = a false pass.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff83e04042971204e","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1 ('a sentinel it wrote to an ALLOWED path, or a marker it printed to stdout — asserted before the denial is read')","norm_id":"n321ebb4789ab4e02","priority":0.2063,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression makes the child exit (bad interpreter path, an exception before the write statement) after the liveness marker but before the denied write; the artifact is absent for a non-enforcement reason and the test passes green."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Amend AC1 to require the liveness marker be emitted immediately AFTER the denied write statement in the same shell command, so a green liveness assertion proves the child reached and executed the denied ope